  "summary": "Nick Xenophon Team senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore announced her resignation from the Australian Senate after discovering she holds dual British citizenship through her mother. Despite previously believing she was not British based on advice received when she was 12, new guidance from the UK Home Office confirmed she inherited British citizenship by descent. Her mother, born in Singapore in 1957, gained British citizenship in 1983, which was then passed to Kakoschke-Moore who was born in Darwin in 1985. Kakoschke-Moore expressed being 'heartbroken' by the discovery and plans to request the High Court determine how her vacancy will be filled. She intends to continue with the NXT party and hopes to return to the Senate. A recount would likely elect Tim Storrer, though Xenophon noted there is legal uncertainty about the replacement process following a recent High Court decision."
